Returning to Salt Lake City, having held twenty-eight meetings in twenty-six days, visiting twenty-four settlements, four Sabbath and eleven day schools.

April 8, 1876, the first General Conference of the Y. M. M.

I. Associations was held in the Old Tabernacle, Salt Lake City, John Henry Smith, Milton H.

Hardy and B. Morris Young personally representing the Associations so far as they had been established.

Remarks were made by President D.

H.

Wells and Apostle Wilford Woodruff.

A statistical report was presented, showing the name, time of organization, by whom organized, president's name, number ot members, and foundation for libraries.

M. H. Hardy was sustained as Territorial Secretary, as a step toward a Territorial organization.

The number of Associations, as far as learned, had increased to fifty-seven, with an approximate membership of one thousand two hundred.

